🌱 Biology: systemic analogue
Let’s reframe in biology:
Vitality (V) = Biomass × (Metabolic-speed²)
Biomass (m) → embodied substrate (cells, tissues, ecological matter).
Metabolic speed (c) → rate of biochemical flows (ATP turnover, nutrient cycling, oxygen exchange).
Metabolic-speed² (c²) → recursive amplification through feedback loops (enzymes, gene regulation, ecological interactions).
Vitality (V) → biological energy available for growth, adaptation, reproduction.
💡 Interpretation: Biology translates the law into life-capacity: substrate mass × amplified process-speed = vitality.
